# Local build and boot

- Compile with RosBE. The first boot config is GCC, i386, Debug, target `bootcd`.
- `tools/pipeline/Build-Bootcd.ps1` writes `build/bootcd.iso`.
- `tools/pipeline/Test-Boot.ps1` runs `C:\Program Files\qemu\qemu-system-i386.exe -accel tcg -m 8192 -smp 4`. This QEMU binary has no WHPX. Windows 10 22H2 boots use the same memory and CPU count.
- Load `tools/qemu-harness/abi.dll` with `-plugin`. It logs `SYSENTER`, `SYSCALL`, `INT 2E`, and calls into mapped `ntoskrnl`, `hal`, and `wdf` exports.
- Serial logs, plugin JSONL, and crash JSON go under `output/`. Do not commit `build/` or `output/`.
- Commands and the WHPX follow-up are in `docs/LOCAL_BUILD.md`.
